abstract: >
  Documentation release for the Heliosonic Sonifier system — a real-time
  NOAA solar wind sonification instrument integrating AI-assisted composition,
  reinforcement learning, adaptive state machines, and a quantum-inspired
  glitch engine. This release includes the full architecture description,
  research context, hardware prototypes, performance benchmarks, and
  transparency statements. Source code and executables are proprietary and
  not distributed.

